Types of project management plans

Linear // Initiation -> Planning -> Execution -> Control -> Closure

This plan is traditional, the plan stays thes same throughout your project [GANTT chart]

Iterative // Multiple sprints, so small linear plans. Which rapidly creates a basic product, then build on it

This plan is common in software dev, as you can build a basic simulation then build on it

Exploratory // Evaluate landscape -> Identify leads - > Assess leads -> Deploy lead

This is for novel science, where there are many routes so you start by evaluating landscape

Overall how to plan iterative/exploratory

Gantt chart to capture high level milestones
Need a dynamic tool to manage scope within sprints, plan made at start of sprint which can be modified
Kanban used to coordinate activities within the sprint
Scope for later sprints undefined

Rolling wave // Put in place high level milestones -> only do detailed plans up to early milestones -> later milestone plan changed later on

Ie. if lit review + 3 materials synthesised. MAke lit review + 1st material plan, then 2 other materials aren't planned
Use a kanban for day to day tasks
